        "parms": "# pgmin, rtin and sysexin — programs, clock and SysEx\npgmin reports program changes as 1-128, the numbers most devices show, with the channel. rtin reports the real-time bytes a sequencer or drum machine sends to keep others in time: 248 is a clock tick, 24 to a quarter note, 250 start, 251 continue, 252 stop and 255 reset. sysexin sends every byte of a system-exclusive message, from 240 to 247, and nothing else.\nThe first argument is the input port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. A port that cannot be opened, or no keyboard at all, leaves the object silent, and the patch still loads. On Windows a port can be open in one place at a time, so untick it under Settings › MIDI for a patch to hear it.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
